{"step_index":407,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T06:04:30Z","input_tokens":2537,"cache_read_tokens":174254,"output_tokens":2533,"thinking":"The system reports the target device driver is installed, despite previous failures to detect it. Investigating the update process, specifically the conditions that might have prevented detection of this device before. Examining the script lines that control the device interaction to identify possible causes for the initial failure.\n\n\nThe initial detection relies on a specific Product ID. The script's logic wasn't triggered because the device enters a short-lived \"InUsbBurn\" state during boot. This state's brief duration, combined with the query and refresh delays of Windows WMI, causes a timing mismatch, missing the detection window. The update process uses a different library, suggesting an alternative detection mechanism that bypasses the WMI query, making it effective.\n\n\nThe update process utilizes a direct USB scan through a different library, bypassing the problematic WMI-based detection. Specifically, `update.exe` invokes `AmlScanUsbX3` within `AmlUsbScanX3.dll` for USB communication in a significantly faster timeframe. This faster communication is key because it stops the hardware watchdog. This direct, rapid communication ensures the device remains in \"InUsbBurn\" mode (WorldCup) for an extended period, which we want.\n\n\nIn \"InUsbBurn\" mode, `update.exe` directly flashes partitions, including environment variables, configurations, and various image files. Examining the commands, the unlock process explicitly modifies environment variables related to locking and USB settings. This enables flashing of critical partitions, potentially bypassing normal bootloader restrictions. The system appears capable of both direct flashing and transitioning to an unlocked fastboot mode, based on environment configuration.\n\n\nThe update process directly flashes a comprehensive set of partitions, including critical components such as environment configurations, recovery images, and boot images, using specific filenames. It sets environment variables to unlock the device, enabling fastboot mode with a designated PID and \"unlocked: yes\" status. This unlocks fastboot's ability to flash crucial Android system images. It appears we have the required files to attempt this operation.\n\n\nThe system retains a cached USB handle for the device after a reboot, leading to incorrect fastboot state detection. This ghost device prevents accurate connection state reporting, even after the device has rebooted and is no longer in fastboot mode. I will test a command to retrieve the bootloader version using `Invoke-FastbootSafe` to see if the cached handle interferes with a fastboot command.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"Copy-Item \"c:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\FIRMWARE_COMPLETO_B866V2_FASTBOOT\\env_unlocked.img\" \"c:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\programa perfecto\\5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2\\\" -Force\nCopy-Item \"c:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\FIRMWARE_COMPLETO_B866V2_FASTBOOT\\bootloader.img\" \"c:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\programa perfecto\\5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2\\\" -Force\nCopy-Item \"c:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\FIRMWARE_COMPLETO_B866V2_FASTBOOT\\misc_clean.img\" \"c:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\programa perfecto\\5_FIRMWARE_SEGURO_B866V2\\\" -Force\nCopy-Item \"c:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\FIRMWARE_COMPLETO_B866V2_FASTBOOT\\*.dll\" \"c:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\programa perfecto\\1_HERRAMIENTAS_MOTOR\\\" -Force\nWrite-Output \"Copied missing firmware and DLL files successfully.\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Copy env_unlocked.img, bootloader.img, and DLLs to programa perfecto"}}]}
